### On-demand retrieval of upstream source tarballs.
###
### Source tarballs are not stored in this repository. sources/manifest.txt
### records the upstream URL and SHA-256 of each one, and the rule below
### fetches and verifies any that are missing.
###
### Each Makefile.<pkg> includes this file and lists its tarball as a
### prerequisite of its configure- target, so a missing tarball is downloaded
### as an ordinary part of the build. Fetching one by hand also works:
###
###     scripts/fetch-source.sh Python-3.14.3.tar.xz
###     scripts/fetch-source.sh --all

FETCH_SOURCE	= scripts/fetch-source.sh

### Only fires for files that do not already exist, so a tarball that is
### present (or checked in, as with spark and maxima-kernel) is left alone.
sources/%:
	@${FETCH_SOURCE} $*

### make treats files built by a pattern rule as intermediate and deletes them
### once the build is done. These are expensive to re-download, so keep them.
.PRECIOUS: sources/%
.SECONDARY: sources/%
